│                          │ every candidate move) and stalls immediately, producing a near-zero minimum area. Two     │
│                          │ targeted improvements: (1) vectorize the minimum-area computation with NumPy (compute all │
│                          │ 165 triangle areas at once via a precomputed index array), and (2) replace the fragile    │
│                          │ greedy step with a fixed-seed simulated-annealing-style random search that perturbs one   │
│                          │ random point at a time and accepts moves that increase the minimum area (plus rare uphill │
│                          │ moves early on). This explores the configuration space far more effectively while keeping │
│                          │ determinism via a fixed RNG seed. Early-exit is kept for speed.                           │
