│ patch_description        │ The current function returns all zeros, giving a min area of 0. I propose a two-stage     │
│                          │ deterministic constructor: (1) initialize with a hand-designed, symmetric configuration   │
│                          │ known to be strong for the Heilbronn problem in an equilateral triangle (vertices + edge  │
│                          │ midpoints + a coarse interior lattice, which spreads points evenly and avoids tiny-area   │
│                          │ triplets), and (2) refine it with a deterministic, seeded coordinate-descent hill climb   │
│                          │ that maximizes the minimum triangle area over all C(11,3)=165 triplets, while keeping     │
│                          │ every point inside the triangle via half-plane constraints. The min-area is computed      │
│                          │ vectorized for speed, and the whole refinement is bounded in iterations so eval_time      │
│                          │ stays modest. Determinism is guaranteed with a fixed RNG seed; failure of the optimizer   │
│                          │ cannot make things worse since perturbations are only accepted when they strictly improve │
│                          │ the objective.                                                                            │
