│ patch_name               │ softmin_coarse_multistart_hard_polish                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current program optimizes the hard min-area objective from a single handcrafted seed, │
│                          │ which gets stuck: the min-area landscape is highly degenerate (many flat plateaus), and   │
│                          │ single-coordinate random moves rarely escape poor basins. Two expert-motivated changes:   │
│                          │ (1) a soft-min (log-sum-exp over the smallest 15-25% of the 165 triangle areas) coarse    │
│                          │ phase, which gives a smooth gradient-like signal to escape plateaus and lift many small   │
│                          │ triangles simultaneously, followed by the hard min objective for fine polishing; (2)      │
│                          │ deterministic multi-start over several structured seeds (perturbed lattices, edge-heavy   │
│                          │ layouts) with the best result kept, giving better basin coverage. Areas are cached        │
│                          │ per-iteration in vectorized form (only 165 triplets, cheap). Final greedy                 │
│                          │ coordinate-pattern polish squeezes out remaining slack. Determinism preserved via fixed   │
│                          │ seeds and fixed iteration counts.                                                         │
