│ patch_description        │ The current program scores 0.00 because `_min_triangle_area` contains a syntax/attribute  │
│                          │ bug: `i, j, k = np.triple = np.array(...).T` attempts to assign an attribute on the numpy │
│                          │ module (`np.triple = ...`), which raises AttributeError since modules do not allow        │
│                          │ arbitrary attribute assignment. The function crashes on every call, so the whole          │
│                          │ constructor fails and returns nothing valid.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fix: (1) rewrite `_min_triangle_area` cleanly with precomputed triplet index arrays       │
│                          │ (computed once, cached), which also speeds up the optimization dramatically compared to   │
│                          │ rebuilding index lists each evaluation; (2) replace the fragile seed + slow               │
│                          │ coordinate-descent with the recommended multi-start annealed hill-climb: several          │
│                          │ deterministic starts (hand-designed symmetric seed, triangular-lattice seed,              │
│                          │ hexagonal-like seed, plus several Dirichlet-random barycentric samples from a fixed RNG), │
│                          │ each given a short annealed schedule with barycentric folding to maintain feasibility,    │
│                          │ followed by a fine polish of the best result. Folding via barycentric clamping guarantees │
│                          │ all points stay inside the triangle, removing the need for the `_inside` rejection logic. │
│                          │ All randomness is seeded, so the function is deterministic.                               │
