│ patch_name               │ group_moves_annealing                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation notes that single-point moves plateau around min_area ≈ 0.02 (well     │
│                          │ below the known ~0.037 optimum) because individual perturbations cannot escape local      │
│                          │ optima where the minimal-triangle constraint involves tight clusters of points. I add a   │
│                          │ simulated-annealing refinement phase that (a) with ~25% probability perturbs 2–3 nearby   │
│                          │ points simultaneously with correlated Gaussian deltas scaled to the current step size,    │
│                          │ and (b) accepts uphill moves with a standard Metropolis criterion. This lets coordinated  │
│                          │ clusters shift together. To keep the evaluator's normalization convention untouched (it   │
│                          │ normalizes by the triangle area itself), we keep raw areas. The annealing runs after the  │
│                          │ hard polish, uses a wall-clock budget for robustness, and the best-ever configuration is  │
│                          │ always kept, so failures degrade gracefully to the previous pipeline output.              │
