╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ projected_subgradient_ascent                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of returning empty points, this approach treats Heilbronn placement as continuous │
│                          │ maximin optimization: it starts from a deterministic low-discrepancy (golden-ratio)       │
│                          │ initialization inside the triangle, then runs a projected maximin local ascent. At each   │
│                          │ iteration it computes the smallest-area triangle, computes numerical gradients of that    │
│                          │ area w.r.t. each point (only the constraining triplet matters), moves all points to       │
│                          │ increase the minimal area, and projects points back into the triangle via barycentric     │
│                          │ coordinates. Multiple deterministic restarts (fixed seeds) are used and the best          │
