│ patch_name               │ annealed_softmin_kick_repolish                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current optimizer plateaus around a local optimum of the hard-min objective. Two      │
│                          │ targeted fixes, following the recommendation:                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Annealed soft-min**: The soft objective currently uses a fixed sharpness k=200 and   │
│                          │ frac=0.15. Sharpening the surrogate progressively (k annealed from 150 to 600) and        │
│                          │ widening the fraction to 0.20 lets Phase 1 lift more near-minimal triangles               │
│                          │ simultaneously and smoothly transition toward the hard-min Phase 2, rather than abruptly  │
│                          │ switching objectives.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Kick-and-repolish**: After greedy polish converges to a hard-min local optimum,      │
│                          │ small random "kicks" (deterministic seed) applied to the points of the minimal triangle   │
│                          │ followed by re-polish escape shallow local optima. This is a well-known basin-hopping     │
│                          │ technique for the Heilbronn problem, since the objective is piecewise (the identity of    │
│                          │ the minimal triangle changes discretely).                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 4                                                                                         │
