│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_seed_startup_and_validation                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Two targeted improvements:                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Multi-seed initialization.** The current heuristic hand-crafted seed can start the   │
│                          │ annealing in a poor basin. Known good Heilbronn configurations for n=11 place most points │
│                          │ on the triangle boundary (vertices and edge subdivisions) with a few interior points. We  │
│                          │ add several structured candidate seeds (boundary-heavy layouts with different             │
│                          │ subdivisions and interior placements), evaluate each with the exact hard-min objective,   │
│                          │ and start the optimizer from the best one. This costs microseconds at module-call time    │
│                          │ but can shift the whole search into a better basin, directly raising min_area.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Validation harness before return.** Following the recommendation from prior          │
│                          │ generations (Gen 35's syntax-error 0.00, Gen 7/27 exceptions), we add a lightweight       │
│                          │ self-check that the output has shape (11,2), finite values, distinct points, and lies     │
│                          │ within the triangle, falling back to a safe clipped configuration otherwise. Correctness  │
│                          │ dominates algorithmic gains; this guards the score against regressions.                   │
