│ patch_name               │ directed_normal_polish                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Add a deterministic directed polish phase after Phase 4. It sweeps the ~10 smallest       │
│                          │ triangles in ascending area order; for each binding vertex it probes moves along the      │
│                          │ outward normal of the opposite edge (analytically: rotate the edge vector by 90°,         │
│                          │ oriented away from the vertex), with step-halving on failure. This targets exactly the    │
│                          │ binding constraints, complementing the existing stochastic polish (which Gen 31 showed    │
│                          │ fails by moving only within the minimal triangle). Random kicks (20% budget) retain       │
│                          │ exploration. For the smallest triangle {i,j,k}, moving vertex i along the outward normal  │
│                          │ of edge (j,k) increases that triangle's area at the maximal local rate (gradient          │
│                          │ direction of |cross|), so a halving search from step 0.01 converges quickly to any        │
│                          │ available improvement. Repeat sweeps until no sweep improves.                             │
