│ patch_name               │ adopt_best_pipeline_anneal_temp                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.80) uses a monolithic annealing loop with a `softmin`        │
│                          │ surrogate that only smooths triangles within 5% of the minimum — a very narrow, brittle   │
│                          │ landscape. The best prior program (score 0.82) uses a multi-start pipeline:               │
│                          │ `_soft_search` (soft-min over the smallest 15% of triangles, temp=200) → `_hard_refine` → │
│                          │ `_directed_polish` → `_pair_exchange`, with structured seeds. I adopt that pipeline       │
│                          │ wholesale and apply the recommended landscape improvement: anneal the soft-min            │
│                          │ temperature progressively (temp = 50·(1+5·it/iters), i.e. 50→300) inside `_soft_search`.  │
│                          │ A low initial temp gives a smooth, gradient-rich landscape (the near-minimal set          │
│                          │ dominates gently), while the sharpening schedule makes the surrogate converge toward the  │
│                          │ hard minimum before the Phase 2 hard refinement takes over, smoothing the soft→hard       │
│                          │ transition. This changes only the landscape geometry, not the acceptance logic            │
│                          │ (keep-if-improved), which prior generations showed is the right acceptance scheme. All    │
│                          │ seeds and the RNG are deterministic (seed 20240517), preserving reproducibility, and the  │
│                          │ try/except fallback to `_lattice_seed` provides graceful error handling.                  │
