│ patch_description        │ Instead of blind random-walk simulated annealing that moves arbitrary points (wasting     │
│                          │ moves on points that don't affect the bottleneck), this approach: (1) uses barycentric    │
│                          │ coordinates for exact, clean feasibility projection into the equilateral triangle, (2)    │
│                          │ targets perturbations only at points participating in the currently smallest triangle —   │
│                          │ the active constraint — which is the key efficiency gain, (3) runs a short multi-start    │
│                          │ over several structurally diverse seeds (vertex+edge-heavy, hexagonal-ring rotated 30°,   │
│                          │ and perturbed-lattice) with two-stage screening, and (4) uses an adaptive step schedule   │
│                          │ with restarts from the incumbent. This concentrates search effort where the objective is  │
│                          │ actually determined, escaping lattice-seeded local basins and yielding far larger minimum │
│                          │ areas.                                                                                    │
